  <div class="manifesto-inner">
    <div class="manifesto-label">Why we built this</div>
    <h2 class="manifesto-headline">Feed readers don't think.<br>Briefly does.</h2>
    <div class="manifesto-body">
      <p>Feedly shows you articles. The Rundown gives you headlines. ChatGPT answers questions you already know to ask.</p>
      <p>None of them tell you what a piece of news <em>means for your business</em> — specifically, practically, today.</p>
      <p>That's the gap Briefly fills. Every story comes with a "so what" — a plain-English take on what you should notice, what you should do, and why it matters to you and not just the market in general.</p>
      <p>For decades, that kind of opinionated, personalized intelligence belonged to people who could afford analysts and research teams. We think every founder deserves it — at a price that doesn't require a Series B to justify.</p>
    </div>
